From 5f70401033a5047e47f502cfd2bda52a807dd8f6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Usty <usty@uase.tech>
Date: Tue, 25 Aug 2026 07:20:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix: icon alignment, bigger touch targets, and inline comment
 box on the feed (follow-up to item A.1)

Direct feedback fixes on the icon redesign shipped last batch:

1. Icon alignment bug (root cause): car-info-top used
   align-items:flex-end, anchoring the icon stack to the bottom of
   the row - whose height varies by how much detail text a card has
   (city/state present or not). Icons floated at different heights
   card to card. Fixed with flex-start, so icons now consistently
   start at the same line as the car name on every card.

2. Bigger, more tappable icons - increased icon size, added real
   padding for a proper touch target (32x32px minimum), bumped count
   text size.

3. Inline comment box, opened from tapping the comment icon - type
   and post a comment without leaving the feed, plus a 'View N
   comments' link to jump to the full thread. Real structural issue
   caught and fixed before this landed: the whole card was a <Link>
   (renders as <a>), and nesting interactive form elements inside an
   anchor is invalid HTML and risks the click firing navigation
   instead of the input. Restructured so the card is now an outer
   div containing the Link (for navigation) as a sibling to the
   comment box, not nested inside it.

4. Scroll-to-comments on the detail page: the new 'View comments'
   link passes ?scrollTo=comments, and the detail page scrolls there
   automatically once loaded, via a new commentsRef + effect gated
   on the loading state so it never fires before content is
   rendered.
